From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:31:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Add the S_UART0 controller

The SoC dtsi describes no UART of the CPUS domain. A board that brings
S_UART0 out on a pin header cannot use it.

Add S_UART0 at 0x07080000 (A733 manual, memory map), interrupt SPI 201
(12.2.3.1). The manual gives all its UARTs one register list (18.10.8),
so the node is a DesignWare APB UART like the ones in the CPUX domain. It
has a bus gate and a reset in the PRCM (4.2.5.15); the baud rate comes
from the bus clock (18.10.3), so there is no module clock.

Add the pin group for TX/RX on PL6/PL7, function 3 (18.14.3.1), which the
Radxa Cubie A7S routes to pins 13 and 15 of its pin header. The pins are
shared with S_SPI0 and S_IR_RX, so a board uses one function on them. The
node is disabled; a board enables it.

Not covered: DMA requests, and flow control.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: with the node enabled for a test and pins 13
and 15 of J11 joined, the bytes sent on PL6 come back on PL7 and raise
the port interrupt.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index 7087c4d4e69e..65c169758266 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -1834,6 +1834,13 @@ r_pwm_pm4_pin: r-pwm-pm4-pin {
 				allwinner,pinmux = <6>;
 				function = "s_pwm0";
 			};
+
+			/omit-if-no-ref/
+			r_uart0_pl6_pins: r-uart0-pl6-pins {
+				pins = "PL6", "PL7";
+				allwinner,pinmux = <3>;
+				function = "s_uart0";
+			};
 		};
 
 		r_ir: ir@7040000 {
@@ -1854,6 +1861,17 @@ pck600: power-controller@7060000 {
 			#power-domain-cells = <1>;
 		};
 
+		r_uart0: serial@7080000 {
+			compatible = "snps,dw-apb-uart";
+			reg = <0x07080000 0x400>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 201 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>;
+			reg-shift = <2>;
+			reg-io-width = <4>;
+			clocks = <&r_ccu CLK_BUS_R_UART0>;
+			resets = <&r_ccu RST_BUS_R_UART0>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
 		r_i2c0: i2c@7083000 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-i2c",
 				     "allwinner,sun8i-v536-i2c",
